cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the mitoxdi tool, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Cell composition and cell-death signatures in sepsis and acute respiratory distress syndrome: analysis code and mitoxdi"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, governance artifacts and the standalone mitoxdi tool accompanying a study of
  composition deconfounding in critical illness. Bulk cell-death transcriptomic signatures in
  sepsis and acute respiratory distress syndrome are largely explained by leukocyte composition;
  suppression of monocyte and macrophage mitochondrial and ER-mitochondria contact transcripts
  survives composition control. mitoxdi re-scores any published signature against its own
  composition-only null.
